        "original_id": "e4c49b66-f6d1-5ef2-a447-a0124b32a94e",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Plants: Monstera, Cercis, Monstera acuminata\n- Taxonomy: Araceae, Fabaceae, Cercidoideae\n- Places: the Americas, tropical regions, warm temperate regions, central Petén, San Luis Potosí\n\nFacts:\n- Monstera is a genus of about 50 species of flowering plants in the arum family Araceae and is native to tropical regions of the Americas.\n- Cercis is a genus of about 10 species in the subfamily Cercidoideae of the pea family Fabaceae and is native to warm temperate regions.\n- Monstera acuminata is abundant in central Petén and extends north to San Luis Potosí, making it the northernmost Monstera species.",
